{{inh+|es|la|ambō|ambōs|g=m-p}}. Old Spanish consistently had {{m|osp|amos}}, representing the inherited form, while {{m|roa-ole|ambos}} existed in neighbouring Old Leonese. Later, Latin influence helped {{m|es|ambos}} spread into Spanish as well, where it displaced the form without /b/.

